# Credentials. Never commit these. The 0600 mode on disk is the first line of
# defence and this file is the second; neither is a substitute for the other.
*.env
*.curl
*.token
kaggle.json
application_default_credentials.json
*.pem
service-account*.json

# Regenerated by Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw dataset files. uci/ IS committed -- it is what explicit_specs.py and
# stratum_d.py read.
#
# This block said "not needed to reproduce any number in the paper" until
# 2026-08-22. That was FALSE for stratc_data/: two of section 6.4's three
# downstream arms read it, and with the directory excluded their figures rested
# on a frozen text file nobody could regenerate -- which is the exact failure
# this paper criticises elsewhere. Re-running the arm found cirrhosis had
# drifted (oracle 0.703 -> 0.699) and nobody could have known.
#
# bikesharing.csv is 1.1 MB and is now committed, below. Klaverjas2018.arff is
# 164 MB and stays out; fetch_stratc_data.py restores it from OpenML 41228
# against a recorded SHA256 and rebuilds the documented seed-0 subsample.
leakage-benchmark/memcheck_csv/
# NOTE the trailing /* : excluding the DIRECTORY makes the negation below
# inert, because git will not descend into an excluded directory to re-include
# a file inside it.
leakage-benchmark/stratc_data/*
!leakage-benchmark/stratc_data/bikesharing.csv
leakage-benchmark/pdfs/
leakage-benchmark/*.csv
# ...except the three intermediate result tables the paper's own tables are
# built from. These are outputs, not downloads: losing them means re-running
# the forests and the bootstrap to get them back.
!leakage-benchmark/downstream2.csv
!leakage-benchmark/confusion.csv
!leakage-benchmark/baseline10_features.csv
# ...but datasets/ is the shipped corpus, not scratch data.
!leakage-benchmark/datasets/MANIFEST.csv

# Rendered on demand by pagecount.py
*_body.pdf
.pagecount_*

# Pre-git hand snapshots. Git is the history now.
*.bak
*.bak_*

# Uncompressed sweep caches — the .gz forms are committed instead, and
# restore_caches.sh puts these back.
leakage-benchmark/hf_meta/cards.json
leakage-benchmark/kaggle_meta/full.json
leakage-benchmark/kaggle_meta/deep_index.json
leakage-benchmark/openml_meta/features.json
